gfg:- Sort a linked list of 0s, 1s and 2s

question:-

Given the head of a linked list where nodes can contain values 0s, 1s, and 2s only. Your task is to rearrange the list so that 
all 0s appear at the beginning, followed by all 1s, and all 2s are placed at the end.

exmaple:-
Input: head = 1 → 2 → 2 → 1 → 2 → 0 → 2 → 2
   
Output: 0 → 1 → 1 → 2 → 2 → 2 → 2 → 2


solution:-

class Solution {
public:
    Node* segregate(Node* head) {
        Node* dummy1 = new Node(0);
        Node* one = dummy1;
        Node* dummy2 = new Node(0);
        Node* two = dummy2;
        Node* dummy3 = new Node(0);
        Node* three = dummy3;

        Node* curr = head;
        while (curr != NULL) {
            Node* nextNode = curr->next;
            curr->next = NULL;

            if (curr->data == 0) {
                one->next = curr;
                one = one->next;
            }
            else if (curr->data == 1) {
                two->next = curr;
                two = two->next;
            }
            else {
                three->next = curr;
                three = three->next;
            }

            curr = nextNode;
        }
        one->next = (dummy2->next) ? dummy2->next : dummy3->next;
        two->next = dummy3->next;

        return dummy1->next;
    }
};